    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters July 3rd with a clear offensive engine led by **James Wood** (74.31) and **Brice Turang** (73.74). **James Wood** earns the premier spot today, benefiting from an elite xwOBA profile and a favorable matchup against Mitch Keller; batting atop the order provides the volume necessary to exploit this efficiency. Simultaneously, **Brice Turang** serves as our primary catalyst for stolen bases, maintaining a high floor against Jose Cabrera. While **Mickey Moniak** (69.90) lacks a confirmed opposing starter, his projected efficiency is buoyed significantly by a high-value park factor (+14%), making him a strong start despite the uncertainty. **Isaac Paredes** (67.73) and **Max Muncy** (64.22) round out our most potent infield options, with both players seeing their scores elevated by positive SP skill matchups against Nick Martinez and Tyler Phillips, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (51.97), who flirted with the final utility slot but ultimately lost out due to a combination of a challenging left-on-left platoon disadvantage and a looming 38% rain risk. While **Travis Bazzana** provides high-upside speed, the optimizer favored the safer floor of **Kyle Karros** (52.22), whose park-adjusted projection remained more stable. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno** (43.71) and **Corbin Carroll** (52.12); both are tagged to face Kyle Harrison, whose elite 2.97 xERA creates a significant drag on their output. While **Corbin Carroll** remains in the lineup due to his game-breaking stolen base potential, his score reflects the reality of facing a high-skill arm. Managers should closely monitor the official lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, and the rest of the squad, as we remain in \"Lineup Pending\" mode for every slot.",
